+        "family": "exact Q-index of a complete multipartite graph",
+        "n": n,
+        "parts": part_count,
+        "interval_bits": bits,
+        "adjacency_rows": rows,
+        "answer": answer,
+    }
+
+
+def render(inst):
+    n = inst["n"]
+    part_count = inst["parts"]
+    width = (n + 3) // 4
+    lines = [
+        "Compute the signless Laplacian spectral radius of this graph exactly.",
+        "",
+        "Definitions and promises.",
+        f"The simple undirected graph has vertices 0 through {n - 1}.",
+        "Its adjacency matrix A has A[i,j]=1 exactly when vertices i and j are adjacent, and A[i,i]=0.",
+        "The diagonal degree matrix D has D[i,i] equal to the number of neighbors of vertex i.",
+        "The signless Laplacian is the integer matrix Q=D+A, and q(G) is the largest real eigenvalue of Q.",
+        f"This graph is promised to be complete {part_count}-partite: its vertices split into {part_count} nonempty independent parts, every two vertices in different parts are adjacent, and all part sizes are distinct. The parts themselves are not supplied.",
+        "",
+        "Exact adjacency data.",
+        "Row i below is a hexadecimal bit mask for row i of A. Bit j (the coefficient of 2^j, with vertex 0 the least-significant bit) is A[i,j]. Leading hexadecimal zeros are included only for alignment.",
+    ]
+    for vertex, row in enumerate(inst["adjacency_rows"]):
+        lines.append(f"  {vertex}: {row:0{width}x}")
+    denominator = 1 << inst["interval_bits"]
+    height = (1 + 2 * n) ** part_count
+    lines.extend(
+        [
+            "",
+            "Required witness.",
+            "Return q(G) as one JSON object with exactly this shape:",
+            '  {"minpoly":[c0,c1,...,cr],"interval":[[a,d],[b,d]]}',
+            f"Here r={part_count}. The list is the primitive monic minimal polynomial c0+c1*x+...+cr*x^r over the integers, in constant-to-leading order, so cr=1 and |ci|<={height}.",
+            f"The interval is open: a/d < q(G) < b/d. Use the fixed positive denominator d=2^{inst['interval_bits']}={denominator} for both endpoints, with 0<=a<b<=2*n*d. The interval must contain exactly one root of the minimal polynomial, and that root must be its largest real root.",
+            "All integers are written in ordinary base 10. Coefficient order matters. The two rational endpoint pairs are [numerator,denominator]; no decimal approximations are accepted.",
+            "",
+            "Give your final answer inside <answer></answer> tags, as the single JSON object just specified.",
+            'Example syntax: <answer>{"minpoly":[-2,0,1],"interval":[[1,1],[2,1]]}</answer>',
+            "Output nothing else inside the tags.",
+        ]
+    )
