codex
Local G1–G8 now pass on the preserved implementation. The required external hardening is currently blocked for an objective reason: all four script-owned OpenRouter redraws returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded (total limit),” so none counts as an oracle failure and no hardness verdict can honestly be claimed. The module and README record that pending state instead of fabricating G9 evidence. I’m completing a final static audit while the overlapping writer exits; I’ve already identified one citation-number correction to make (the current v2 source labels the new signless blowup result Theorem 2.4, not 2.3).
exec
/bin/bash -lc 'sleep 10; if [ -d /proc/2492641 ]; then echo builder_running; else echo builder_done; fi; tail -50 codex_run.log' in /home/gson/gvrepo/results/2507.02263
codex
The local package is now internally consistent, including an honest `integer_tuple` certificate label and answer-size measurement using the same JSON separators as `emit.sh` (440 characters / 110 estimated tokens). Since the quota failure is fast and deterministic, I’m also invoking the hinted and placebo harnesses in isolated scratch directories so their script-owned failure records are preserved rather than leaving ambiguous missing files.
