codex
Implemented a self-contained Track B generator based on the paper’s Theorem 2.4 and its \(K_4[t]\) blowups.

Key results:

- G1–G8 pass.
- Five heuristic attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Reference extractor: 8/8, 4,632 operations.
- Compact dual-covector route: 8/8, 240 operations.
- Random guessing: 0/200,000.
- Answer size: 440 characters, 48 atoms.
- G9 remains pending because every OpenRouter call returned HTTP 403: “Key limit exceeded (total limit).” No oracle failure was falsely recorded.

Files:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2507.02263/gen_2507_02263.py)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2507.02263/README.md)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2507.02263/selftest_report.json)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2507.02263/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2507.02263/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2507.02263/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The result is correctly marked non-shippable until OpenRouter quota is restored and the three oracle arms produce scored attempts. The source paper is [arXiv:2507.02263](https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.02263).
